@include ../../shared/squash.overtone

## Backhand straight drives
Backhand straight drives, five minutes. A racket length off the side wall, at the back of the
service box. Control first: medium pace, just above the service line, with the first bounce in the
service box, so it comes up to you. Stay behind the ball, no T. Then length, then tight, as I call
them.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 5:00
0:00 [go]
7% Racket up early. No wrist twist.
20% Use the space. Don't crowd the ball.
33% Now length. A racket head above the service line, first bounce behind the service box.
45% Aim higher, not harder.
57% Lost the rhythm? Higher and softer to reset.
67% Now tight. Every one within a racket length of the side wall. Count them in tens.
80% Grip. Prep. Rotate. Swish. Follow.
90% Close to the wall, not on it.
-0:10 Ten seconds.
---
[stop]
